From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: give a visual style's menu bars XP's default height

Purpose: plain Win32 menu bars as tall as XP's under Luna.
XP behavior: with Luna, SPI_GETNONCLIENTMETRICS reports iMenuHeight 19 at
96 DPI on English and Japanese XP, one more than the classic theme's 18,
and 24 at 120 DPI (Japanese XP); a larger menu font raises it (English XP:
Tahoma 8 and 10pt give 19, 12pt gives 21). Luna's ini sets no
MenuBarHeight, and the flat menu setting does not change it.
Wine before: applying a theme kept the classic height, 18 with English
XP's Tahoma 8pt (Japanese XP's MS UI Gothic happened to give 19 at 96 DPI)
and 23 instead of 24 at 120 DPI.
Change: the theme's metrics start from a menu bar height of 19 at 96 DPI,
which the theme's MenuBarHeight replaces and SPI_SETNONCLIENTMETRICS
raises for the menu font, as before. The classic theme keeps its saved
metrics.
Evidence: tests/menu-height.c on the English XP reference (normal, large
and extra large font sizes; flat menus on and off) and on Wine; the
Japanese XP's 120 DPI values from tests/dpi-metrics.c.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL, when a visual style's metrics are
applied.
---
 dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
index 3bf3a0b..4e92c09 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -797,6 +797,11 @@ static inline void parse_init_nonclient (struct PARSENONCLIENTSTATE* state)
         &state->metrics, 0);
     SystemParametersInfoW (SPI_GETICONTITLELOGFONT, sizeof (LOGFONTW),
         &state->iconTitleFont, 0);
+    /* XP gives a visual style's menu bars 19 pixels at 96 DPI unless the
+     * theme sets MenuBarHeight (Luna does not); a taller menu font still
+     * raises it, as SPI_SETNONCLIENTMETRICS does for the classic height. */
+    if (win4wine_external_shell())
+        state->metrics.iMenuHeight = 19;
 
     SetThreadDpiAwarenessContext(old_context);
 }
